<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<shelfDocument>
  <!--
    tooandflow shelf — one tool, modifier-aware.
    See toolbar/tooandflow.shelf in the repo for source.
  -->

  <toolshelf name="tooandflow" label="tooandflow">
    <memberTool name="tooandflow_flipsave"/>
    <memberTool name="tooandflow_copsave"/>
  </toolshelf>

  <tool name="tooandflow_flipsave" label="Flipsave" icon="tooandflow_flipsave">
    <helpText><![CDATA[#icon: MISC_play
#context: scene

= tooandflow Flipsave =

One-click flipbook + dated hip copy. Modifier keys pick the format.

* Click          : MP4 (h264, slow preset, CRF 16)
* Shift + click  : JPG image sequence
* Ctrl + click   : EXR image sequence

Output goes to:
  $HIP/flipbook/YYYY_MMDD/<scene>/<scene>_YYYY_MMDD_<roman>.{hiplc,mp4,jpg,exr}

The dated hip and the render share the same roman tag so they're easy to pair.
]]></helpText>
    <script scriptType="python"><![CDATA[
from tooandflow import flipsave

if kwargs.get("ctrlclick"):
    fmt = "exr"
elif kwargs.get("shiftclick"):
    fmt = "jpg"
else:
    fmt = "mp4"

flipsave.run(fmt)
]]></script>
  </tool>

  <tool name="tooandflow_copsave" label="COP Flipsave" icon="tooandflow_copsave">
    <helpText><![CDATA[#icon: MISC_present
#context: cop

= tooandflow COP Flipsave =

Select any Copernicus node (or a copnet), click. A temp rop_image is
created, rendered over the playbar range at 1080x1080, then removed —
no manual ROP setup. A dated hip copy is saved alongside.

* Click          : MP4 (h264, slow preset, CRF 16)
* Shift + click  : JPG image sequence
* Ctrl + click   : EXR image sequence (linear, pipeline-grade)
* Alt + click    : GIF (palette-optimised, 540x540 @ 15fps)

Output goes to:
  $HIP/flipbook/YYYY_MMDD/<scene>/<scene>_YYYY_MMDD_<HHMMSS>.{hiplc,mp4,gif,jpg,exr}
]]></helpText>
    <script scriptType="python"><![CDATA[
from tooandflow import copsave

if kwargs.get("ctrlclick"):
    fmt = "exr"
elif kwargs.get("shiftclick"):
    fmt = "jpg"
elif kwargs.get("altclick"):
    fmt = "gif"
else:
    fmt = "mp4"

copsave.run(fmt)
]]></script>
  </tool>
</shelfDocument>
